From 40b75b4f3433cb611bb3550a8d75c9575122d699 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Polari Suite <polari@localhost.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:02:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] polari-block pt-2: the pinbank - pad levels from the
 layout's roles, the pin channel, GPIO_IN = level AND input enable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A `pinbank` device resolves each role to its STORED field per pin (an alias-only role, edge_flag = STATUS_W1TC,
through acts_on) and recomputes every pad after each write and each outside input (PIN_TWIN_PLAN.md §2):
- drives when the pad function is one of the pad's GPIO functions, the route is the plain GPIO out and the
  output is enabled; with that route the enable is GPIO_ENABLE whatever OEN_SEL says (an inference from
  ESP-IDF's working path, now measured: the IDF build (OEN_SEL 0) and the HAL build (OEN_SEL 1) both drive);
- open drain drives only 0; inversion of value / enable applied; else the outside level, else the pull, else z;
- a peripheral route on a GPIO pad is logged unmodelled (the light firmware: GPIO4, signal 9).
-global polari-block.chardev=ID: out "@<virtual ns> <pin> 0|1|z" (every pad at reset, then each change), in
"<pin> 0|1|z". The dump adds the pad levels and the edge count. Interrupts are pt-3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/misc/polari_block.c         | 251 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 include/hw/misc/polari_block.h |  30 ++++
